# Admin panel (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/admin-panel.md` and `docs/modules/admin-questions.md`)

`app/admin.py` is ~7.3k lines: grep `@admin_bp.route('<path>'` for the function you need; never read it whole. Routes keyed by `question_id` / taxonomy ids must check the subject explicitly (`_require_md_admin`, `_require_subject_admin`, `_require_taxonomy_admin`) before any capture — the subject decorators refuse (403) without a `subject_id`.

## Panel invariants
- `Subject.id` is immutable; only `name` and `name_zh` are editable. Delete is 400 while any question references it; cleanup order SavedQuestionSet → SavedFilter (JSON `subject` scan) → UserSubjectPermission → `subject_restore_points` → Subject (topics/chapters cascade). Disk is untouched.
- Users: `validate_username` (`^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,80}$`, reserved names); rename moves `User/<old>` → `User/<new>` best-effort; cannot rename, demote, or delete yourself. Your own edit sets the password only. Permissions payload `{"permissions": {sid: role|''|null}}` merges per key.
- Health: `/admin/health/sync?mode=dry_run|delete` (dry run default; 24 h grace for asset-less questions); `/health/stats` is DB-only. Anomaly hand-off to lists via `?qids=` or `?qids_token=<localStorage key>` (consumed once).
- `/admin/ingestion` is a 302 to `/admin/import`; `admin_ingestion.html` no longer exists.
- Super-admin-only pages: Users, Subjects, Settings, LLM Endpoints, Prompts, Health, `/admin/files`.
- Topics / Chapters are **one subject at a time** (`?subject_id=`, session `admin_taxonomy_subject` shared). Do not render every subject's taxonomy on one page.
- Both pages share `partials/taxonomy_admin_js.html` (`oqbTaxonomyAdmin`: SortableJS drag + arrows, double-click inline rename, hide / delete in place). Change behaviour there, not per page; keep the markup contract in its header comment. Its `renumber()` mirrors `utils.number_taxonomy` — change both together.
- `hidden` exists on all four taxonomy levels. Hiding a parent never rewrites its children's flags. Every tag editor fetch (`get_topics` / `get_chapters` / subtopics / subchapters) passes `include_hidden=1`; only the dashboard filter sidebar honours the eye switches.
- `Subject.topic_number_prefix` (default on) / `subtopic_number_prefix` (default off) prefix every teacher-facing topic / subtopic name as plain text (`01 Name`): server `tax_numbers.numbered_name`, client `OQB.taxLabel(node)`. New topic-name displays use those, not bare `display_name` / `node.name`. Display only (never match or post it). Edited via `POST /admin/subjects/<id>/number-prefixes` from the Topics page. Not a restore-point field, and not the Generate-page numbering option.
- Per-row taxonomy edit / toggle-hidden routes call `_require_subject_admin(<row subject>)`; add the same check to any new per-row taxonomy route.
- Every taxonomy level has `name` (English, match key) + optional `name_zh`. Edit routes take either or both (`_taxonomy_name_updates`, validated **before** the restore point); add routes read `_form_name_zh()`; JSON replies use `_taxonomy_json`. Teacher-facing names go through `i18n.display_name`; CSV / AI matching through `i18n.build_name_index`. CSV imports never rename the English name. See `i18n.mdc`.
- **Restore points:** every taxonomy, tag-form, Bulk Edit, CSV import and Auto Tag write calls `subject_snapshot.capture*` **before** its first mutation. New or edited writers must keep that order — see `subject-snapshots.mdc`. `delete_subject` also calls `subject_snapshot.delete_for_subject`.

## Question Management invariants
- Canonical asset path = `_build_asset_file_path`; IMG is multi-part, MD/DOC single-slot (upload rejects a second one; reorder ignores MD/DOC). Asset delete is `POST|DELETE .../assets/<asset_id>/delete`.
- Every IMG/DOC row mutation calls the `doc_thumbnails.on_*` hooks **after commit**; every MD write calls `md_render.invalidate`.
- List filters (`app/question_scope.parse_list_args`): pinned `qids` / `selected_ids` narrow inside the required `subject`; `verified` and `check_status` (+ `check_versions/atypes/formats`, default `TYPED_VERSIONS`) combine.
- Shared Edit modal: `openEditModal(id, {preserveView, preserveAssetScroll})`; hosts define `window.oqbAfterQuestionEdit` and `window.oqbEditNavSource()`; include `edit_question_modal_js.html` only (it pulls `tag_editor_js.html` and `md_editor.html`). Add-question wizard borrows the tag form (`borrowTagFormForAdd` / `returnTagFormToEditModal`). Details tab: breadcrumb, create child (`POST .../children`), set parent (`POST .../parent`), Split link (`GET .../split`, IMG only). Stems cannot be tagged.
- The `/admin/questions` page itself (single-subject tree, bulk panel, `_bulk_subject_guard`) has its own rule: `admin-questions.mdc`.
- QID rename renames files only when `confirm_rename_files` is true.
- `Subject.split_parts_default` is on the Subjects add/edit form and seeds the PDF wizard **Split questions into parts** checkbox.
- Batch ops intersect `question_ids` with `get_user_admin_subjects()` **and** call `_bulk_subject_guard(ids)` (ADR-016). Generate IMG: `find_best_source` DOC > MD, whole-slot `replace_img_assets`, one `word_session` per run, defaults `BATCH_IMG_DEFAULT_WIDTH/STITCH`, accepts `symmetric_horizontal`. Set MCQ ANS: `q_type='MC'`, answer A–D, PNGs from `resources/mcq_answer_img/`, default `versions=EN`. `batch-set-check-state` skips checked slots unless `overwrite`. Batch update (incl. chapters) UI is the **dashboard** Bulk Edit modal: preview (`app/batch_edit.py`) then apply. Do not fork the write off that plan.
- `verified` is a whole-question manual flag independent of per-asset `check_state`; UI soft-warns only.

## Gotchas
- SSE routes gather rows in request context, stream under `app.app_context()`.
- DOC thumbnails are keyed by `asset_id`; changing width needs Health → Force Re-render.
